 "category": "فضاء",
 "topic": "A sugar cube of neutron-star material would weigh about 1 billion tons on Earth (as much as a mountain). Neutron stars are collapsed cores of massive stars, up to about 2 solar masses in a ball about 20 km across; the fastest known spins about 716 times per second.",
 "sources": [
  "https://imagine.gsfc.nasa.gov/science/objects/pulsars1.html",
